// Auto-generated from legacy HTML by scripts/extract-pages.py
export const title = "Counter Statistics Report Format Guide";
export const html = "<h1>Counter Statistics Report Format Guide</h1>\n      <hr class=\"rule\" />\n      <p>Once you've finished the report settings, the statistics report is sent starting from the next scheduled interval.</p>\n      <p>Depending on your settings, the statistics report is sent as CSV- or JSON-formatted data.</p>\n      <p>A single counter can have multiple zones configured. For example, a counter named Counter #1234 could have multiple zones such as Zone #1234, Zone #1235, Zone #1236, and so on.</p>\n      <p>So the format of the sent statistics report varies depending on the counter's configuration.</p>\n      <p>Generally, the statistics report format includes the following data, based on the counter&ndash;zone hierarchy:</p>\n      <ol>\n        <li>Counter-wide aggregate data</li>\n        <li>Per-zone data</li>\n      </ol>\n      <p>Let's walk through the data format sent, using an example.</p>\n\n      <h2>Example Statistics Report Data for the [People Counting] App</h2>\n      <p>Assume the following counter is configured and you're receiving the counter's data periodically via report settings.</p>\n      \n<div class=\"figure\">\n<div class=\"app-panel\" style=\"max-width:480px;\">\n  <div class=\"form-grid\" style=\"grid-template-columns:70px 1fr;font-size:12.5px;\">\n    <span>Name</span><input value=\"Gangnam Station Foot Traffic Counter\" disabled>\n    <span>&#9432; UUID</span><span style=\"font-size:11px;color:var(--text-muted);\">1fe3f8f6-79c9-4451-93dd-8c153653c9cf &#128465;</span>\n  </div>\n  <div style=\"margin-top:10px;\">\n    <div style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:12px;margin-bottom:6px;\">People Counting &nbsp; <span class=\"btn small\">+ Add Zone</span></div>\n    <table class=\"app-table\">\n      <tr><th>Channel</th><th>Name</th></tr>\n      <tr><td>CH 6</td><td>Gangnam Stn. Exit 6 Crosswalk</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>CH 6</td><td>Gangnam Stn. Exit 5 Front</td></tr>\n    </table>\n  </div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n      <p>The counter's name is <strong>Gangnam Station Foot Traffic Counter</strong>, and it has two counting zones configured: <strong>Gangnam Stn. Exit 6 Crosswalk</strong> and <strong>Gangnam Stn. Exit 5 Front</strong>.</p>\n      <p>Adding a report setting in the People Counting app lets you periodically send statistics reports for this counter.</p>\n      <p>Below is an example statistics report configured to send in CSV format on a 5-minute interval.</p>\n\n      <h2>CSV Format Example</h2>\n      \n<div class=\"figure\">\n<pre style=\"background:#0e1420;color:#d7dee8;padding:14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:11px;overflow-x:auto;line-height:1.6;\">timestamp,datetime,[cumulative]-Gangnam Station Foot Traffic Counter,[count]-Gangnam Station Foot Traffic Counter,[A]-Gangnam Station Foot Traffic Counter,[B]-Gangnam Station Foot Traffic Counter,[A]-Gangnam Station Foot Traffic Counter-Gangnam Stn. Exit 6 Crosswalk,[B]-Gangnam Station Foot Traffic Counter-Gangnam Stn. Exit 6 Crosswalk,[A]-...\n1695108000,09/19/2023 16:20:00,46151,263,92,66,74,27,18,39</pre>\n</div>\n\n\n      <h2>JSON Format Example</h2>\n      \n<div class=\"figure\">\n<pre style=\"background:#0e1420;color:#d7dee8;padding:14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;overflow-x:auto;line-height:1.6;\">[{\n  \"timestamp\": 1695109200,\n  \"datetime\": \"09/19/2023 16:40:00\",\n  \"[cumulative]-Gangnam Station Foot Traffic Counter\": 47083,\n  \"[count]-Gangnam Station Foot Traffic Counter\": 234,\n  \"[A]-Gangnam Station Foot Traffic Counter\": 137,\n  \"[B]-Gangnam Station Foot Traffic Counter\": 97,\n  \"[A]-Gangnam Station Foot Traffic Counter-Gangnam Stn. Exit 6 Crosswalk\": 98,\n  \"[B]-Gangnam Station Foot Traffic Counter-Gangnam Stn. Exit 6 Crosswalk\": 38,\n  \"[A]-Gangnam Station Foot Traffic Counter-Gangnam Stn. Exit 5 Front\": 39,\n  \"[B]-Gangnam Station Foot Traffic Counter-Gangnam Stn. Exit 5 Front\": 59\n}]</pre>\n</div>\n\n\n      <p>Each entry includes the following data.</p>\n      <p><strong>Counter aggregation start time</strong></p>\n      <ol>\n        <li><strong>timestamp</strong> &ndash; the Unix Epoch value of the time data collection started.</li>\n        <li><strong>datetime</strong> &ndash; the date and time data collection started, delivered in the format specified under System &ndash; Date &amp; Time settings.</li>\n      </ol>\n      <p><strong>Counter aggregate statistics data</strong></p>\n      <ol>\n        <li><strong>[cumulative]-counter name</strong> (e.g. [cumulative]-Gangnam Station Foot Traffic Counter)\n          <ul class=\"steps\">\n            <li>The total accumulated count value since this counter was last reset.</li>\n            <li>The sum of the accumulated data across every zone configured on the counter.</li>\n            <li>Equal to the previous entry's [cumulative] value plus this entry's [count] value.</li>\n            <li>If a count reset schedule is configured, the accumulated value resets at that time.</li>\n          </ul>\n        </li>\n        <li><strong>[count]-counter name</strong> (e.g. [count]-Gangnam Station Foot Traffic Counter)\n          <ul class=\"steps\">\n            <li>The count this counter tallied during this time window.</li>\n            <li>Equal to the sum of the counts tallied by each zone during this time window.</li>\n          </ul>\n        </li>\n        <li><strong>[A]-counter name</strong> (e.g. [A]-Gangnam Station Foot Traffic Counter)\n          <ul class=\"steps\"><li>The sum of every A-direction count configured on this counter.</li></ul>\n        </li>\n        <li><strong>[B]-counter name</strong> (e.g. [B]-Gangnam Station Foot Traffic Counter)\n          <ul class=\"steps\"><li>The sum of every B-direction count configured on this counter.</li></ul>\n        </li>\n      </ol>\n      <p><strong>Statistics data for the individual zones that make up the counter</strong></p>\n      <ol>\n        <li><strong>[A]-counter name-zone name</strong> (e.g. [A]-Gangnam Station Foot Traffic Counter-Gangnam Stn. Exit 6 Crosswalk)\n          <ul class=\"steps\"><li>The A-direction tally for that zone.</li></ul>\n        </li>\n        <li><strong>[B]-counter name-zone name</strong> (e.g. [B]-Gangnam Station Foot Traffic Counter-Gangnam Stn. Exit 6 Crosswalk)\n          <ul class=\"steps\"><li>The B-direction tally for that zone.</li></ul>\n        </li>\n      </ol>\n\n      <h2>Example Statistics Report Data for the [Vehicle Counting] App</h2>\n      <p>Same report format as the People Counting app.</p>\n\n      <h2>Example Statistics Report Data for the [Occupancy Counting] App</h2>\n      <h3>JSON Format Example</h3>\n      \n<div class=\"figure\">\n<pre style=\"background:#0e1420;color:#d7dee8;padding:14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;overflow-x:auto;line-height:1.6;\">[{\n  \"timestamp\": 1695109200,\n  \"datetime\": \"09/19/2023 16:40:00\",\n  \"[occupancy]-Building Occupancy\": 87,\n  \"[increase]-Building Occupancy\": 3,\n  \"[entry]-Building Occupancy\": 12,\n  \"[exit]-Building Occupancy\": 9,\n  \"[entry]-Building Occupancy-Back Door Entry\": 5,\n  \"[exit]-Building Occupancy-Back Door Exit\": 4\n}]</pre>\n</div>\n\n      <p><strong>Counter aggregation start time</strong></p>\n      <ol>\n        <li><strong>timestamp</strong> &ndash; the Unix Epoch value of the time data collection started.</li>\n        <li><strong>datetime</strong> &ndash; the date and time data collection started, delivered in the format specified under System &ndash; Date &amp; Time settings.</li>\n      </ol>\n      <p><strong>Counter aggregate statistics data</strong></p>\n      <ol>\n        <li><strong>[occupancy]-counter name</strong> (e.g. [occupancy]-Building_Occupancy)\n          <ul class=\"steps\"><li>The occupancy this counter currently computes: total entries minus total exits across every configured zone since the counter was last reset.</li></ul>\n        </li>\n        <li><strong>[increase]-counter name</strong> (e.g. [increase]-Building_Occupancy)\n          <ul class=\"steps\"><li>The change in occupancy this counter tallied during this time window &mdash; the sum of (entries &minus; exits) across every zone configured on this counter.</li></ul>\n        </li>\n        <li><strong>[entry]-counter name</strong> (e.g. [entry]-Building_Occupancy)\n          <ul class=\"steps\"><li>The sum of entries across every zone configured on this counter.</li></ul>\n        </li>\n        <li><strong>[exit]-counter name</strong> (e.g. [exit]-Building_Occupancy)\n          <ul class=\"steps\"><li>The sum of exits across every zone configured on this counter.</li></ul>\n        </li>\n      </ol>\n      <p><strong>Statistics data for the individual zones that make up the counter</strong></p>\n      <ol>\n        <li><strong>[entry]-counter name-zone name</strong> (e.g. [entry]-Building_Occupancy-Back Door Entry)\n          <ul class=\"steps\"><li>The entry tally for that zone.</li></ul>\n        </li>\n        <li><strong>[exit]-counter name-zone name</strong> (e.g. [exit]-Building_Occupancy-Back Door Exit)\n          <ul class=\"steps\"><li>The exit tally for that zone.</li></ul>\n        </li>\n      </ol>\n      <p style=\"color:var(--text-muted);\">TBD.</p>";
